AddRecord 'prop:hajnal' @('PFP.Proposition_4_21','PFP.proposition_4_21','ThesisCommon.IsSetMapping','ThesisCommon.IsSetMappingFree','ThesisCommon.hajnal_of_lt_cofinality','ThesisCommon.hajnal_of_singular','ThesisCommon.hajnal_free_set') 'complete' `
    'For an infinite cardinal kappa and lambda<kappa, every set mapping with values of size strictly below lambda has a free subset of size kappa.' `
    'Both strict cardinal bounds and every infinite ambient cardinal are retained. Maximal free families prove the case lambda<cf(kappa). At singular kappa, actual recursion constructs cofinally growing regular free blocks; a regular-cardinal partition and tail thinning remove both directions of interaction. The cofinal sizes yield a free union of full size. The source cites Hajnal; the checked dependency is expanded using the standard Juhasz Appendix A3.4--A3.5 argument. The reusable helper even permits diagonal values, since freeness concerns distinct points.'
AddRecord 'prop:two-sided-countable-free' @('PFP.Proposition_4_22','PFP.proposition_4_22','ThesisCommon.HasTwoSidedCountableValues','ThesisCommon.twoSided_countable_free_set') 'complete' `
    'For every uncountable cardinal, a set mapping whose values and inverse incidence fibres are countable has a free subset of full cardinality.' `
    'The source transfinite recursion is explicit: each stage avoids previous choices and both incidence unions, whose cardinality is bounded by the cardinality of the initial segment times aleph0, strictly below kappa. The resulting function is injective and its range free. Singular uncountable cardinals are included without any cofinality assumption. Inverse incidence means membership in F(beta), not an equality fibre.'
AddRecord 'rem:omega-one-obstruction' @('PFP.Remark_4_23','PFP.remark_4_23','ThesisCommon.OmegaOneIndex','ThesisCommon.omegaOnePredecessors','ThesisCommon.omegaOnePredecessors_countable','ThesisCommon.omegaOnePredecessors_free_subsingleton') 'complete' `
