AddRecord 'lem:block-decomp' @('PFP.Lemma_4_24','PFP.lemma_4_24','PFP.CoordinateBlockIndex','PFP.IsCountableCoordinatePartition','PFP.EllOneTriangularBlockDecomposition','ThesisCommon.countable_triangular_partition','ThesisCommon.lpBlockCompression_idempotent_of_triangular','ThesisCommon.exists_lp_triangular_countable_blocks') 'complete' `
    'A projection on an ell1 sum with WCG coefficients has a countable-block partition, is triangular in its initial-ordinal order, induces a projection on each diagonal block, and has countably many lower interactions per block.' `
    'Actual outgoing supports are countable by the WCG lemma. The ordinal recursion starts at the first unused coordinate and closes under outgoing interactions through countably many steps outside previous blocks. An injection into a strict initial segment proves exhaustion. Earlier unions are invariant, so actual diagonal block compressions are idempotent. A countable output support meets only countably many disjoint blocks. Every displayed conclusion is proved, including finite and empty index types via permitted empty blocks.'
AddRecord 'lem:large-diagonal' @('PFP.Lemma_4_25','PFP.lemma_4_25','ThesisCommon.lp_exists_large_diagonal_blocks','ThesisCommon.lp_block_diagonal_on_supported_union') 'complete' `
    'Above aleph1, the triangular countable-block decomposition has a full-cardinality family of mutually noninteracting blocks. The displayed diagonal identity holds on every vector supported by their union.' `
