AddRecord 'thm:Jp-dual-primary' @('ThesisCommon.JamesPath','ThesisCommon.HasBoundedJamesVariation','ThesisCommon.JamesSequenceSpace','ThesisCommon.JamesSequenceSpace.variationNorm','ThesisCommon.JamesSequenceSpace.norm_eq_iSup_path_variation','ThesisCommon.JamesSequenceSpace.instCompleteSpace','ThesisCommon.jamesLpInsert','ThesisCommon.jamesLpRead','ThesisCommon.jamesSequence_hasComplementedLp_withBound','ThesisCommon.jamesSequence_everyHyperplane','ThesisCommon.jamesSequence_dual_everyHyperplane','ThesisCommon.JamesSequenceSpace.initial_tendsto','ThesisCommon.jamesSchauderBasis','ThesisCommon.james_functional_initial_tendsto','ThesisCommon.james_bidual_ext_coordinates','ThesisCommon.jamesResiduumScalarEquiv','ThesisCommon.jamesSequence_quasiReflexive_orderOne','ThesisCommon.JamesBlockSum','ThesisCommon.jamesBlockSynthesis_norm_le','ThesisCommon.jamesBlockSynthesis_range_eq_ker','ThesisCommon.jamesBlockDecomposition','ThesisCommon.JamesFiniteSectionSum','ThesisCommon.jamesFiniteSectionAbsorption','ThesisCommon.jamesUniversalFiniteSumAbsorption','PFP.Theorem_B_4_general','PFP.theorem_B_4_general','ThesisCommon.james_scalar_one_factors_with_sampling','ThesisCommon.jamesSequence_hasCPFP_four','ThesisCommon.jamesSequence_primary','ThesisCommon.projection_range_sampling_decomposition','ThesisCommon.jamesAbsorbRetractOfFiniteSectionSum','PFP.Theorem_B_4_classical','PFP.theorem_B_4_classical','PFP.Theorem_B_4','PFP.theorem_B_4') 'complete' `
    'For every finite 1<p, primariness of the actual James sequence space implies primariness of its continuous dual. The dual of the classical James space at p=2 is primary without that premise.' `
    'The actual Bird--Laustsen norm is the supremum of finite increasing-path p-difference norms on null scalar sequences. Its norm laws, coordinate domination and completeness are proved. Even-coordinate insertion and adjacent-difference extraction give an actual complemented lp copy with projection and distortion at most two. Scalar absorption proves that both James space and its continuous dual are isomorphic to all closed hyperplanes. Actual initial truncations are contractive and converge in norm for finite p; this constructs the actual normalized Schauder basis. For 1<p<infinity, actual disjoint-vector estimates prove shrinking and finite dual-coordinate density. The coordinate-limit map on the actual bidual has exactly the canonical image as kernel and is onto the scalar field. Its genuine quotient equivalence proves quasi-reflexivity of order one, and B.3 with the proved hyperplane hypotheses proves the original conditional general-p clause. Actual monotone sampling and repetition give a norm-one step projection. The lp sum of finite-dimensional interval blocks synthesizes with norm at most two and a sharp lower bound, and its exact range is the sampling kernel; this gives an actual James-space/block-sum decomposition. Actual shifts and finite-section equivalences prove absorption of every lp sum of initial James sections, including arbitrary zero-dimensional sections and the standard universal finite-section sum. The scalar character is computed on the actual bidual quotient, and its kernel is exactly the weakly compact operators. Alternating row/prefix selection, summable coordinate errors, an actual diagonal correction and a Neumann inverse give identity factors whose reading map is an invertible correction of coordinate sampling. The remaining projection summand is a bounded retract of that sampling kernel. Shift/drop maps handle an arbitrary first sample, and actual finite-block identifications, dependent lp flattening and repeated finite-section absorption remove the remaining summand. This proves primariness and 4-PFP of the actual James space for every finite 1<p over real or complex scalars, as separately named strengthened results. Specializing primariness to p=2 discharges the classical clause; the original general-p clause retains its printed premise. This explicit sampling-kernel route expands the cited classical input without assuming or claiming the broader classification of all reflexive complemented James subspaces.'
foreach ($row in $rows) {
    if ($row.proof_status.StartsWith('statement only')) { $row.method_status = 'not assessed: main proof open; actual definitions checked' }
    if ($row.id -eq 'thm:Jp-dual-primary') { $row.method_status = 'original clauses complete; cited classical input expanded by actual sampling-kernel absorption; stronger general-p facts separately named' }
    if ($row.id -in @('lem:coordinate-diagonalisation','lem:block-decomp3')) {
        $row.statement_status = 'printed formula preserved; section-context uncountability explicit in separate target'
    }
}
AddRecord 'thm:BlpUPFP' @('PFP.Theorem_5_15','PFP.theorem_5_15','ThesisCommon.exists_lpOperator_matrixProduct_retraction','ThesisCommon.lpOperatorBlockRead_comp_insert','ThesisCommon.lpOperatorSequenceEquiv','ThesisCommon.lpOperatorMatrixEquiv') 'complete' `
    'For every finite 1<p, the actual Banach space of bounded operators on scalar lp has the uniform primary factorisation property.' `
    'Finite initial-corner compression embeds the operator space into the actual bounded matrix product. A scalar hyperfilter limit, with finite lp estimates and coordinate convergence proved, constructs a contractive operator-valued left inverse on every bounded matrix family. Conversely, disjoint infinite lp blocks give actual contractive insertion and reading of the matrix product in the operator space. The bounded product of operator spaces has its own explicit sequence flattening; the checked decomposition method first derives sequence self-similarity of B(lp), then the actual B(lp)-matrix-product equivalence from the two complementary embeddings. This avoids assuming the cited isomorphism or circularly assuming operator-space self-similarity. The proved isomorphic invariance transports UPFP from Theorem 5.14. Both real and complex scalars and the exact original exponent range are retained.'
AddRecord '7.1' @('ThesisCommon.GowersMaurey.ConstructionData','ThesisCommon.GowersMaurey.constructionData_nonempty','ThesisCommon.GowersMaurey.implicitNorm','ThesisCommon.GowersMaurey.implicitNorm_fixed','ThesisCommon.GowersMaurey.implicitNorm_le_of_closed','ThesisCommon.GowersMaurey.ShiftSpace','ThesisCommon.ShiftGowersMaureySpace','ThesisCommon.GowersMaurey.rightShiftIsometry','ThesisCommon.shiftGowersMaureySpace_infiniteDimensional','ThesisCommon.shiftGowersMaureySpace_primary_of_prime','PFP.gowersMaureyConstructionExists','PFP.Example_7_1_named','PFP.Example_7_1','PFP.Example_7_1_all_constructions','PFP.example_7_1_named_iff') 'statement only; actual construction and supporting results complete' `
    'The fixed actual shift-generated complex Gowers--Maurey space is asserted to be prime and hence primary, to have the strictly-singular operator quotient isomorphic as a Banach algebra to ell1(Z) with convolution, to have continuum many maximal operator ideals all containing the strictly singular operators, and to fail PFP.' `
    'The source Section4.2 construction is implemented on finitely supported sequences using the least fixed point of its norm operator and the genuine completion. Rational/Gaussian-rational block lists are countable; a rapidly growing positive sequence and an injective code into its even source subsequence are constructed, so the named space has no assumed existence or operator property. Norm laws, the fixed-point formula, minimality, contractive spreads, the isometric right shift and infinite dimension are proved. Primeness implies primariness by a separately checked general argument, but primeness itself remains an explicit premise and is unproved here. The operator quotient uses actual strictly singular operators, the genuine quotient norm and literal convolution coefficients. The named original target and the stronger all-construction targets remain unproved. Complex scalars are explicit for the unit-circle maximal-ideal assertion; the construction itself supports RCLike scalars.'
$rows[$rows.Count-1].method_status = 'construction and supporting maps checked; main operator-theoretic assertions open'
AddRecord '5.2' @('PFP.Remark_5_2_asPrinted','PFP.Remark_5_2_separable','PFP.remark_5_2_separable','PFP.remark_5_2_separable_same_constant') 'printed assertion unproved; corrected separable version complete' `
    'The printed remark asserts transfer of PFP and UPFP from an arbitrary coefficient space X to C(omega-star,X).' `
    'The printed target is retained on the actual compact Hausdorff free-ultrafilter model of omega-star. Drewnowski1989 Theorem5 (p123) assumes X separable and Y-star weak-star separable; Corollary6 (p124) retains separability of X. The separately named separable version is now proved by actual scalar quotient identification, countable simultaneous stabilization, vector clopen compression and contractive insertion and reading. PFP and UPFP transfer, preserving every supplied C-PFP constant. The citation does not justify the unrestricted printed assertion, which remains open; no counterexample to that assertion is claimed. See PFP-S06.'
$rows[$rows.Count-1].statement_status = 'printed target preserved; cited separability assumption explicit in corrected target'
$rows[$rows.Count-1].method_status = 'cited separable proof expanded on actual omega-star; unrestricted assertion open'
AddRecord '3.4' @('PFP.Remark_3_4','PFP.remark_3_4','ThesisCommon.NormalizedSchauderBasis.SubsymmetricWith','ThesisCommon.NormalizedSchauderBasis.exists_subsymmetric_compression','ThesisCommon.NormalizedSchauderBasis.hasCPFP_of_subsymmetric') 'complete' `
    'A normalized subsymmetric basis not equivalent to ell1 gives UPFP. Actual increasing-subsequence insertion and reading maps replace the isometric maps in the symmetric argument.' `
