AddRecord 'rem:separable-range' @('PFP.Remark_4_5','PFP.remark_4_5','ThesisCommon.ellOne_hasUPFP_of_separable_scalar_ranges','ThesisCommon.ellOne_hasPFP_of_separable_scalar_ranges','ThesisCommon.UncountableSchauderSum.hasUPFP_of_separable_scalar_ranges','ThesisCommon.UncountableSchauderSum.hasPFP_of_separable_scalar_ranges') 'complete' `
    'If every coefficient-to-scalar-coordinate operator has separable range, outgoing coordinate supports are countable. Above aleph1, one-sided Hajnal selection supplies a full-cardinality diagonal coordinate set and the factorisation transfer follows.' `
    'Both the ell1 and general symmetric non-ell1 clauses use the actual scalar spaces and bounded operators. The exact cardinal threshold is retained. Uniform factorisation preserves the coefficient bound; the qualitative branch keeps the source uncountable-cofinality requirement. WCG and a countable total dual set are replaced by the stated separable-range premise, not retained as extra hypotheses.'
AddRecord '4.31' @('PFP.Remark_4_31','PFP.remark_4_31','ThesisCommon.ellOne_countable_outgoing_entries_of_separable_scalar_ranges','ThesisCommon.UncountableSchauderSum.countable_outgoing_entries_of_separable_scalar_ranges') 'complete' `
