$treeRow.correspondence_notes = 'Both actual finite-support segment norms and their genuine completions are constructed separately. Antichain lp estimates and weak nullity prove the analytic pruning steps for every finite p>1. Two-colour descendant selection and summable branch oscillation construct a diagonal multiplier and its actual reciprocal, with reciprocal norm at most three. Support-delayed fork cells give norm-one insertion/readback maps onto the exact selected closed span. Every operator has an arbitrarily close genuine finite-column perturbation, including finite support for the complementary columns. The operator-dependent finite-frontier recursion applies the actual pruning proposition, grafts new roots while preserving processed nodes, and stabilizes into a genuine subtree embedding. It proves small head norms, small connecting-cell masks and exact zero for deeper cells from finite support. Finite readback reconstruction and ordered Schauder convergence give summable column errors with total at most one sixth; no unconditional basis estimate is assumed for the consecutive norm. The reciprocal and Neumann correction give factor bound six for finite-column operators. A genuine norm perturbation below one twelfth removes that restriction and gives uniform factor bound twelve for arbitrary operators. Both unchanged original targets are proved over every RCLike field for all finite p>1, with no selection, support or factorisation premise. The constant twelve is independent of p and is stronger than the asserted existence of C_p. No equivalence between the two norms or unqualified JT_p alias is claimed.'
