$bmRow.correspondence_notes += ' The correct closed-infimum formulation is now checked: for nonnegative C, the infimum is at most C exactly when actual isomorphisms have distortion at most C+epsilon for every positive epsilon. The paper wrapper specializes C>=1. This does not assume or claim attainment at C; the printed endpoint reverse implication remains separately open.'
